  "family_proof": "The quadratic kernel K is span(p=ab,Q), with polar ranks0,2,6,8. Thus its intersection with a full-rank quadratic field target containingQ is exactlyspanQ. Three remaining gates are rank-tight. A first new field direction would have a quadratic product residue t moduloK with t,t+Q both rank8. Every residue coset has a K-corrected member of rank<=4; the other pair members differ only by rank2 p, so this is impossible. Both complete scans explicitly check all four K offsets, including zero. Invertible affine input maps preserve degree filtration and polar rank and must transport the whole target jointly. Operand constants add old wires only.",
  "cone_requirement_dependency": "Under the Q-by-four exclusion, every one of the first5 gates must reach the selected scalar decoder. Otherwise its at-most4-gate ancestor cone can be scheduled first, contradicting that branch exclusion. Syntactic reachability is necessary but not a proof of semantic minimality.",
